<title>USA: MoneyGram links stock drop to downgrade.</title>
<headline>MoneyGram links stock drop to downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A MoneyGram Payment Systems Inc spokesman on Thursday said a sharp drop in the company's share price was likely prompted by Montgomery Securities' downgrading of the stock.</p>
<p>Montgomery in a research report lowered its rating on the stock to near-term hold from buy, citing concerns over MoneyGram's earnings.</p>
<p>The shares closed on Thursday at 9-7/8, extending a decline that began the previous session, when it dropped more than 23 percent from 13.</p>
